[
    {
        "id": "tab6310001",
        "type": "tab",
        "label": "1 - Ingest & produce",
        "disabled": false,
        "info": "Nano 33 BLE Sense (USB serial) -> Node-RED parses each line, runs a rolling-window vibration check, and produces onto two Redpanda topics:\n  imu.raw    - every sample\n  imu.alerts - only samples the vibration check flagged\n\nEdit the serial-port config node's port to match `ls /dev/tty.*` (macOS/Linux) or your COM port (Windows) before deploying. This tab also carries the two DB-polling widgets on the Live dashboard page (the ax/ay/az chart and row count), which read imu_samples back the same way a real dashboard would - by querying the database, not by tapping the serial line directly."
    },
    {
        "id": "tab6320002",
        "type": "tab",
        "label": "2 - Consume imu.raw -> TimescaleDB",
        "disabled": false,
        "info": "An independent consumer, its own consumer group (`ts-writer`), reads topic imu.raw and writes every sample into the imu_samples hypertable. It knows nothing about tab 1's producer or tab 3's alert consumer - stop this flow, the producer and the alerts path keep running, Redpanda holds every message this consumer has not yet read."
    },
    {
        "id": "tab6320003",
        "type": "tab",
        "label": "3 - Consume imu.alerts -> DB + live dashboard",
        "disabled": false,
        "info": "A second, separate consumer (`alert-writer` group) reads topic imu.alerts. Each alert is written to imu_alerts AND pushed straight to the Live dashboard's alert table in the same step - the live feed is not a database poll, it is the stream itself reaching the screen. The History page's alert table is the same data read back out of TimescaleDB on a timer, the serving-layer view of the same events."
    },
